+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                               DAN                                 |
|       a tiny scripts used to ease your dotfile management         |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
Dan is a very minimal dotfile manager with purpose for personal use.
If you found it useful, don't hesitate to leave a star!


=== Features
============
Here are some of the features we had for now. These may change over
time as the project grows and develops:

  - Sync

  - Apply

  - Sync all

  - Apply all

  - Remove

  - List


=== Background
=========
I'm a person who often reinstall the OS, just because it feels slow.
That's the reason why i need a dotfile manager. I've used stow, but
it doesn't fit with my use case. I don't like the system it uses,
symlinking folder and files. I prefer copy-paste system. That's when
this program first written.
The code is heavily inspired by my previous attempt to create the
simple dotfile manager, DotMan.
But it had too many bugs, so i rewrite it. And here we are with it,
a minimal script that can manage your dotfiles.


=== Installation
================
Here are some installation tutorial step-by-step for some Operating
Systems:

  - Linux
  You need to have bash, git and make installed on your system.
  Step-by-step installation on linux:

    - Open your terminal, and then paste command below (one by one)

    - git clone https://github.com/potydon/dan; cd dan

    - sudo make install


  - Windows 11
  You need to have powershell and git installed on your system.
  Step-by-step installation on windows 11:

    - Open your windows terminal / command prompt, then paste These
      command below

    -	git clone https://github.com/potydon/dan; cd dan

    -	./install.ps1


